For 4.5 request_attention + WindowControlArea:
- request_attention trait: doc L838, default empty L839. X11 impl 1535-1541 (early return if active; set_wm_hints_urgency true). set_wm_hints_urgency helper 392-423: read existing WM_HINTS, preserve, skip clear if not urgent (avoid creating property + round trip), write back, flush. Clear on activation: state refresh 1137-1141 — comment explains urgency has no withdrawal signal; focus is conventional means. Windows impl 837-856: FlashWindowEx FLASHW_ALL once, also early-return when active. Wayland: empty (1588) — comment in activate (1571-1586) explains KWin/Mutter can use app_id for attention indication via activation token instead.
- Lifecycle diagram: 调用 request_attention → (inactive) → set urgency → WM 闪烁任务栏 → 用户点击窗口 → _NET_WM_STATE 变化 → refresh_window_state → was_active=false→active=true → clear urgency.
- WindowControlArea enum (window.rs:737-748): Drag/Close/Max/Min. Used by on_hit_test_window_control callback (platform.rs:859): GPUI registers (window.rs:1751-1766) a closure that checks rendered_frame.window_control_hitboxes against mouse_hit_test — i.e., 应用把自绘的关闭/最大化/最小化按钮区域上报给平台，平台在原生命中测试（如 X11 的 _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE 或 Wayland 的 decorations 协商）时询问。Also app-side window.window_controls() (2574-2576) and Linux-specific window_decorations (2559-2561), trait Linux block: window_controls default WindowControls::default() (platform.rs:926-928).

